course: dictionary
lesson: 3744
title: Flower: a thing or an action
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). The words around it show which. «On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower» uses flower as a thing you can land on. «The tree flowers in spring» uses flowers as an action: the tree makes flowers.
explain: Look for clues. Words like «a», «a bunch of» and «wild» before the word show it is a thing. A word for what someone or something does, like «the tree», shows it is an action. Check by swapping in another word, such as bloom, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Flower also means a plant grown for its flowers, as in «a flower bed». Context tells you which meaning is in use.
fact: A flower is the coloured part of a plant that blooms, like a rose or a tulip.
fact: To flower means to make flowers, and it is a verb.
fact: In science, a flower's job is to make seeds.
fact: Pollination is when pollen from one flower reaches the middle part of another flower of the same kind; bees often help carry it.
fact: «Flower» can also mean a plant grown for its flowers, as in «wild flowers».
exercise: On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower. What is a flower in this sentence? | A thing that moves through the sky | A kind of seed | *A coloured part of a plant that blooms | A sort of bee
exercise: «The tree flowers in spring.» What kind of word is flowers here? | A number | A noun: a thing you can pick | An adjective: it describes the tree | *A verb: the tree makes flowers
exercise: Which phrase means a plant grown for its flowers? | Flower in the sky | Flowering hour | *Flower bed | Bunch of flowers
test: A flower's job is to make seeds. What is pollination? | Grass growing taller | Bees eating nectar | *Pollen reaching the middle part of a flower, usually from another flower of the same kind | Petals falling off in the wind
test: «Sunflowers live for one summer.» What is their natural life? | *They grow, flower, make seeds and die | They flower every year for a hundred years | They never make seeds | They live only in winter
exam: In «No Mow May» asks people to skip mowing so flowers can bloom, what does bloom mean? | To die |  | *To open and show colour | To grow tall | To be cut down
